  "text": "NICE Guideline CG150: Headaches in Over 12s Diagnosis and Management | Publisher: National\nTension-Type Headache Self-Care and Management\nTension-type headache is the most common primary headache disorder,\ncharacterized by a dull, aching band-like pain across the forehead or back\nof the head.\nSelf-Care & Non-Pharmacological Management: - Stress Management: Cognitive\nrelaxation, biofeedback, and regular physical rest. - Hydration:\nMaintaining adequate fluid intake throughout the workday. - Posture &\nErgonomics: Ensure proper screen height and chair support to prevent neck\nmuscle strain. - Limit Medication Use: Avoid taking acute pain medicines\nfor more than 10-15 days per month to prevent medication-overuse headache\n(MOH).\nPage 1 of 4 | Official Educational Resource",
